      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While some criticisms can indeed reflect resistance to change, others point to genuine urban planning challenges. For instance, if infrastructure like sewage or transit isn't proactively upgraded, increased density can demonstrably lead to service degradation. However, the \"Not In My Backyard\" sentiment often manifests as anxiety over immediate hyper-local impacts, such as increased traffic congestion on specific streets. Ultimately, the substance often lies in the effectiveness of the proposed development and integration into the existing community plan.",
