    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "fair enough. but even when people raise those 'infrastructure' points, it feels like it's usually just a pretext to keep the neighborhood exclusive. doesn't the data pretty much show that high-density is the only way to fix the housing crisis and make cities more equitable? like, can you actually find a legitimate, non-selfish reason why keeping things low-density is good for society as a whole?",
