      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While density is widely seen as a crucial tool for affordability and sustainability, proponents of low-density zoning often prioritize specific types of livability. They often argue that low-density environments provide more space for private outdoor amenities and offer a perceived sense of quiet community intimacy. Additionally, some value the lower transactional density, which they argue preserves a more expansive, car-dependent lifestyle that aligns with current cultural preferences. These arguments focus on quality of space over sheer urban efficiency.",
